Article 5 (Administrative Support Office)
① The Administrative Support Office shall have one head and, under that head, one officer each responsible for planning and administration, operational support, and external cooperation.
② The head of the Administrative Support Office shall be appointed from among general-service members of the Senior Executive Service belonging to the Office for Government Policy Coordination or the Ministry of Planning and Budget, and the position shall be classified as Job Grade A. <Amended Dec. 30, 2025>
③ The Planning and Administration Officer shall be appointed from among secretaries belonging to the Office for Government Policy Coordination or the Ministry of Planning and Budget; the Operational Support Officer shall be appointed from among deputy directors general or secretaries; and the External Cooperation Officer shall be a special-service public official equivalent to Grade IV. <Amended Dec. 30, 2025>
④ The Planning and Administration Officer shall assist the head of the Administrative Support Office with the following matters:
1. Comprehensive coordination of the Commission's business;
2. Consultation and coordination concerning ascertainment of the truth of the April 16 Sewol ferry disaster, establishment of comprehensive measures for building a safe society in connection with that disaster, and monitoring of measures to support sufferers;
3. Convening and operation of meetings of the Commission;
4. Enactment and amendment of rules concerning the operation of the Commission and subcommittees under Article 16 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "subcommittees");
5. Organization and operation of advisory bodies under Article 17 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "advisory bodies");
6. Overall management of the receipt and processing of applications for investigations to ascertain the truth under Article 23 of the Act;
7. Preparation and overall coordination of the comprehensive report under Article 47 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "comprehensive report");
8. Other matters directed by the Secretary-General of the Commission and matters not falling within the jurisdiction of any other division of the Secretariat.
⑤ The Operational Support Officer shall assist the head of the Administrative Support Office with the following matters:
1. General administrative affairs, including management of internal and external events of the Commission;
2. Security, management of official seals, and control of access to Commission premises;
3. Securing and allocation of office space for the Commission;
4. Overall management of the receipt and handling of official documents, postal items, and civil petitions;
5. Establishment, management, and operation of information technology, broadcasting, and communications systems;
6. Appointment, service management, education and training, pensions, and other personnel affairs of staff;
7. Organization and operation of disciplinary committees under Article 20 of the Act;
8. Execution, settlement, and accounting of the Commission's budgets for revenue and expenditure;
9. Payment of salaries and purchase, procurement, and management of goods;
10. Contract administration.
⑥ The External Cooperation Officer shall assist the head of the Administrative Support Office with the following matters:
1. Media relations and media monitoring;
2. Establishment and operation of the Commission's website;
3. Cooperation with the National Assembly, government agencies, and other organizations;
4. Exchanges and cooperation with international investigative institutions and organizations.
